# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's host-gap package WPH (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. WPH/ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag the pack's B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# H1 (FIRST, card M only, soft): WPH-3 on ONE card (optimisation/ttnn-op/batched_reads): the verify and collect read-backs read three ways - the served per-shard blocking to_torch,
# one mesh-composed to_torch a tensor (QWEN_FAST_BATCHED_READS=1) and non-blocking copy_device_to_host_tensor into host tensors allocated once and one fence (=async) - compared as bit patterns against
# the served read, then timed (400 serpentine rounds a set; the verify set is 2 tensors, the collect set one quad's 5). It settles, BEFORE any four-card time, that the three pinned bindings exist and accept the
# real shapes, dtypes and layouts, that the bytes are the same, and which variant to run. A card sees one chip: the four-chip composition is the audited attach's and the ABAB's job; the report PROJECTS the
# four-chip cost by the arithmetic it prints (served = chips x the one-shard read; the batched paths = their one-shard read + 3 extra enqueues a tensor) and names no more than that.
# READ: 'BATCHED_READS verdict=PASS' (exit 0: every path that ran is byte-exact; FAIL names the set and the tensor; NOT-RUN carries the error), the 'BATCHED_READS timing_verdict compose=... async=...' line,
# 'BATCHED_READS async_parts' (q, the enqueue of one copy, and the fence), the projected line, and 'BATCHED_READS pick reads=1|async|none'. DECISION (ORDER.txt): pick 1 -> the -fx-wph-all profiles; pick async ->
# the -fx-wph-all-async ones; pick none or a FAIL -> WPH-3 is out of the arms (run H2 and H3 alone). A path that raised is its own error line and does not fail the other. Duration (estimate): 25 minutes (container
# timeout 1 h; the per-call watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only). CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/batched_reads/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--rounds 400
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
